## Context

Author directive, 2026-10-26:
- verify-gate MUST reuse previous check, gate and adherence results;
- the checks it runs reflect what the diff touches, and it states what it tests and why before running them;
- integration testing is out of scope by default.

Today `skills/verify-gate/SKILL.md:147` says "Check, gate and adherence
results are never reused", so every round re-runs everything whatever the diff
touched. Incident: JETP-observer PR #240 (tickets/ and STATE.md only) re-ran
the full fast suite on every pushed head for a one-line ticket-log fix.

Related: [[1100]] (reuse/invalidation tied to revisions and affected scope),
[[1219]], [[1221]].

## Exit criteria

- [ ] verify-gate reuses a prior check, gate or adherence result when its recorded head or base is unaffected by the diff since then, and records each reuse with the result's source and head; the "never reused" rule is gone.
- [ ] Before running anything, the gate prints a plan: each check it will run or reuse, and why, derived from the paths the diff touches (for example: tickets/ only → `erg check`, no test suite).
- [ ] Integration tests are out of scope by default; a gate runs them only when the diff touches what they cover, or when the caller or project explicitly asks for them, and says which.
- [ ] A regression covers (a) a ticket-only diff that reuses a prior green result and runs only the ticket check, and (b) a code diff that invalidates the reuse.
- [ ] The harness gate (`.merge-gate.json` checks) passes.
